 "intro": "Atuatuca, the winter camp of a legion and a half in the land of the Eburones, northern Gaul, winter 54 BC. You are the legates Sabinus and Cotta. King Ambiorix has warned you that Gaul is rising, and offers you safe passage.",
 "debrief": "In Caesar’s account, Sabinus wanted to accept Ambiorix’s offer and Cotta to stay in the camp; Sabinus prevailed after a night of argument. The column marched out laden with baggage and was ambushed in a deep valley. The Romans formed a circle while the Eburones threw javelins and fell back from every charge. Sabinus went to parley and was killed; Cotta died fighting. The eagle-bearer threw the eagle inside the rampart, and the last survivors killed themselves that night. Caesar is said to have sworn not to cut his hair until he was avenged. The other choices are what-ifs.",
