   "title": "A friendly warning",
   "text": "You are the legates Quintus Titurius Sabinus and Lucius Aurunculeius Cotta, wintering at Atuatuca with a legion and a half. Ambiorix, king of the Eburones, who owes Caesar favours, warns you that all Gaul is rising and the Germans are crossing the Rhine. He offers you safe passage to the next camp.",
   "intel": {
    "hint": [
     {
      "text": "Why would an enemy warn you?"
     }
    ],
    "scout": [
     {
      "text": "Stay behind your rampart; you have food and walls."
     }
